  "id": "cap0073-sac-trust-creates-trustline-signed-header",
  "title": "SAC trust() creates a trustline with no ChangeTrust and no event (SIGNED header arm)",
  "description": "An InvokeHostFunction operation calls trust(address) on a Stellar Asset Contract. The operation meta shows a created TrustLineEntry with limit INT64_MAX; the operation emits no contract event. A reader that keys trustline handling on ChangeTrust operations or on events sees nothing. Same ledger and transaction as cap0073-sac-trust-creates-trustline, from the previous recording of the stellar-core golden: the header's StellarValue uses the SIGNED arm instead of SIGNED_MS, so readers built on XDR without that arm can decode it.",
